GIVEN `the row` IS A `A row of the permanent injury tables`
GIVETH A `A part of the tables`
`the part of the tables for` `the row` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the row`
    WHEN `total and incurable blindness of both eyes` THEN `total permanent injury`
    WHEN `total and incurable mental disorder` THEN `total permanent injury`
    WHEN `loss of both arms or both hands` THEN `total permanent injury`
    WHEN `total deafness of both ears` THEN `total permanent injury`
    WHEN `removal of the lower jaw` THEN `total permanent injury`
    WHEN `loss of speech` THEN `total permanent injury`
    WHEN `loss of one arm and one foot, one arm and one leg, one hand and one leg, or one hand and one foot` THEN `total permanent injury`
    WHEN `loss of both legs or both feet` THEN `total permanent injury`
    WHEN `loss of part of the skull, through its full thickness, over more than 6 cm2` THEN `partial permanent injury, the head`
    WHEN `loss of part of the skull, through its full thickness, over 3 cm2 to 6 cm2` THEN `partial permanent injury, the head`
    WHEN `removal of part of the lower jaw, of a whole branch of the upper jaw, or of half the upper jaw` THEN `partial permanent injury, the head`
    WHEN `loss of one eye` THEN `partial permanent injury, the head`
    WHEN `total deafness of one ear` THEN `partial permanent injury, the head`
    WHEN `loss of more than 8 teeth that cannot be replaced by dentures` THEN `partial permanent injury, the head`
    WHEN `loss of 5 to 7 teeth` THEN `partial permanent injury, the head`
    WHEN `loss of 3 to 4 teeth` THEN `partial permanent injury, the head`
    WHEN `loss of 1 to 3 teeth` THEN `partial permanent injury, the head`
    WHEN `loss of an arm or a hand` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `loss of the main part of the bone of the upper arm` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `complete paralysis of the upper arm` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `complete paralysis of the circumflex nerve` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `ankylosis of the shoulder` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `ankylosis of the elbow in a favourable position` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `ankylosis of the elbow in an unfavourable position` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `loss of the main part of both bones of the forearm` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `complete paralysis of the median nerve` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `complete paralysis of the radial nerve in the arm` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `complete paralysis of the radial nerve in the hand` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `complete paralysis of the ulnar nerve` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `ankylosis of the wrist in a favourable position` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `ankylosis of the wrist in an unfavourable position` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `amputation of the whole thumb` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `amputation of the whole index finger` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `amputation of the thumb and the index finger together` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `amputation of the thumb and one finger other than the index finger` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `amputation of 3 fingers including the thumb` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `amputation of 3 fingers other than the thumb and the index finger` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `amputation of 4 fingers including the thumb` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `amputation of 4 fingers other than the thumb` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `amputation of one finger other than the thumb and the index finger` THEN `partial permanent injury, the upper limbs`
    WHEN `amputation of a thigh, upper half` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `amputation of a thigh, lower half` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `total loss of a foot, by tibio-tarsal disarticulation` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `partial loss of a foot, by sub-talar disarticulation` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `partial loss of a foot, by medio-tarsal disarticulation` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `partial loss of a foot, by tarso-metatarsal disarticulation` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `complete paralysis of a lower leg` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `complete paralysis of the external popliteal nerve` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `complete paralysis of the internal popliteal nerve` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `complete paralysis of both the internal and external popliteal nerves` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `ankylosis of the hip` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `ankylosis of the knee` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `loss of most of the femur or of most of both bones of the lower leg` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `loss of most of the kneecap, in many fragments, hindering movement between lower leg and thigh` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `loss of most of the kneecap, movement still possible` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `shortening of a leg by at least about 5 cm` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `shortening of a leg by 3 to 5 cm` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `amputation of 4 toes including the big toe` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `amputation of 3 toes including the big toe` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`
    WHEN `amputation of the big toe` THEN `partial permanent injury, the lower limbs`

§§ `The upper-limb columns, and the left-handed insured`

-- The upper-limb table prints a rate for the right side and one for the left. For a
-- left-handed insured the columns are swapped.
-- src:413 | Khi Người được bảo hiểm là người thuận tay trái, tỷ lệ bồi thường đối với tay được áp dụng theo cách
-- src:414 | ngược lại, tức là tỷ lệ áp dụng cho tay phải lúc này sẽ áp dụng cho tay trái và ngược lại.
@ref src 413-414; fork F6 (NOTES.md): the swap applies to every row printed with two columns
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`whether the insured is left-handed is not in the record, and the rate for an arm or hand turns on it` MEANS
    REFUSE "whether the insured is left-handed is not in the record, and the rate for an arm or hand turns on it"

GIVEN `the side`          IS A `A side of the body`
      `the right column`  IS A NUMBER
      `the left column`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the column read for` `the side` `, the right column being` `the right column` `and the left` `the left column` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the side`
    WHEN `the right side` THEN `the right column`
    WHEN `the left side`  THEN `the left column`

GIVEN `the printed rate` IS A `The printed rate`
      `the side`         IS A `A side of the body`
      `left-handed`      IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate read from` `the printed rate` `for the side` `the side` `and left-handedness` `left-handed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the printed rate`
    WHEN `one rate` r THEN r
    WHEN `a rate for each side` `right column` `left column` THEN
        CONSIDER `left-handed`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `whether the insured is left-handed is not in the record, and the rate for an arm or hand turns on it`
        WHEN JUST lh THEN
            IF lh
            THEN `the column read for` `the side` `, the right column being` `left column` `and the left` `right column`
            ELSE `the column read for` `the side` `, the right column being` `right column` `and the left` `left column`

§§ `Rows found from a count or a measurement`

-- Teeth (src 371-374). Four bands: more than 8 teeth that cannot be replaced by dentures; 5 to
-- 7; 3 to 4; 1 to 3. Three teeth are in two bands (fork F7: the first band printed, 3 to 4,
-- which is also the higher rate). Exactly 8 teeth are in no band, and neither are more than
-- 8 teeth that dentures can replace (NOTES.md, Findings).
-- src:371 | * Mất răng trên 8 cái không lắp được răng giả 30%
-- src:372 | * Từ 5 – 7 răng 15%
-- src:373 | * Từ 3 – 4 răng 8%
-- src:374 | * Từ 1 – 3 răng 3%
GIVEN `the number of teeth`          IS A NUMBER
      `can be replaced by dentures`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `A row of the permanent injury tables`
`the row for the loss of` `the number of teeth` `teeth, replaceable by dentures:` `can be replaced by dentures` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of teeth` GREATER THAN 8 AND NOT `can be replaced by dentures` THEN JUST `loss of more than 8 teeth that cannot be replaced by dentures`
        IF `the number of teeth` AT LEAST 5 AND `the number of teeth` AT MOST 7      THEN JUST `loss of 5 to 7 teeth`
        IF `the number of teeth` AT LEAST 3 AND `the number of teeth` AT MOST 4      THEN JUST `loss of 3 to 4 teeth`
        IF `the number of teeth` AT LEAST 1 AND `the number of teeth` AT MOST 3      THEN JUST `loss of 1 to 3 teeth`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Skull (src 362-365): loss of part of the skull through its full thickness, over more than
-- 6 cm2, or from 3 cm2 to 6 cm2. Under 3 cm2 is in no band.
-- src:362 | * Mất một phần xương sọ với toàn bộ bề dày của
-- src:363 | xương:
-- src:364 | * - mất với diện tích trên 6cm2 40%
-- src:365 | - mất với diện tích từ 3cm2 tới 6cm2 20%
GIVEN `the area` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `A row of the permanent injury tables`
`the row for the loss of part of the skull, in square centimetres:` `the area` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the area` GREATER THAN 6                          THEN JUST `loss of part of the skull, through its full thickness, over more than 6 cm2`
        IF `the area` AT LEAST 3 AND `the area` AT MOST 6     THEN JUST `loss of part of the skull, through its full thickness, over 3 cm2 to 6 cm2`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Shortening of a leg (src 445-447): "at least about 5 cm", and "3 to 5 cm". Exactly 5 cm is
-- in both (fork F8: the first band, "at least", which is also the higher rate); "about" is
-- read as no tolerance. Under 3 cm is in no band.
-- src:445 | * Chân bị hụt đi ít nhất khoảng 5cm
-- src:446 | 30%
-- src:447 | * Chân bị hụt đi từ 3 đến 5cm 20%
GIVEN `the shortening` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `A row of the permanent injury tables`
`the row for the shortening of a leg, in centimetres:` `the shortening` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the shortening` AT LEAST 5                              THEN JUST `shortening of a leg by at least about 5 cm`
        IF `the shortening` AT LEAST 3 AND `the shortening` AT MOST 5 THEN JUST `shortening of a leg by 3 to 5 cm`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Fingers of one hand (src 403-411). Nine rows. Which set of fingers each row prices:
--   the whole thumb; the whole index finger; thumb and index together; the thumb and one
--   finger other than the index; 3 fingers including the thumb; 3 fingers other than the
--   thumb and the index (so: middle, ring and little); 4 fingers including the thumb;
--   4 fingers other than the thumb; one finger other than the thumb and the index.
-- Of the 31 possible sets of whole fingers, 10 are in no row: any 2 fingers without the
-- thumb, 3 fingers that include the index but not the thumb, and all 5 (NOTES.md, Findings).
-- src:403 | * Cụt toàn bộ ngón cái 20% 15%
-- src:404 | * Cụt toàn bộ ngón trỏ 15% 15%
-- src:405 | * Cụt đồng thời ngón cái và ngón trỏ 35% 25%
-- src:406 | * Cụt ngón cái và ngón khác ngoài ngón trỏ 25% 20%
-- src:407 | * Cụt 3 ngón trong đó có ngón cái 35% 30%
-- src:408 | * Cụt 3 ngón trừ ngón cái và ngón trỏ 20% 15%
-- src:409 | * Cụt 4 ngón trong đó có ngón cái 45% 40%
-- src:410 | * Cụt 4 ngón trừ ngón cái 40% 35%
-- src:411 | * Cụt một ngón ngoài ngón cái và ngón trỏ 10% 5%
GIVEN `the fingers` IS A LIST OF `A finger`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A row of the permanent injury tables`
`the row for the amputation of the fingers` `the fingers` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF n EQUALS 1 AND `with the thumb`                        THEN JUST `amputation of the whole thumb`
        IF n EQUALS 1 AND `with the index finger`                 THEN JUST `amputation of the whole index finger`
        IF n EQUALS 1                                             THEN JUST `amputation of one finger other than the thumb and the index finger`
        IF n EQUALS 2 AND `with the thumb` AND `with the index finger` THEN JUST `amputation of the thumb and the index finger together`
        IF n EQUALS 2 AND `with the thumb`                        THEN JUST `amputation of the thumb and one finger other than the index finger`
        IF n EQUALS 3 AND `with the thumb`                        THEN JUST `amputation of 3 fingers including the thumb`
        IF n EQUALS 3 AND NOT `with the index finger`             THEN JUST `amputation of 3 fingers other than the thumb and the index finger`
        IF n EQUALS 4 AND `with the thumb`                        THEN JUST `amputation of 4 fingers including the thumb`
        IF n EQUALS 4                                             THEN JUST `amputation of 4 fingers other than the thumb`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        n MEANS count (nub `the fingers`)
        `with the thumb` MEANS elem `the thumb` `the fingers`
        `with the index finger` MEANS elem `the index finger` `the fingers`

-- Toes of one foot (src 448-450): 4 toes including the big toe; 3 toes including the big
-- toe; the big toe. No row prices a toe other than the big toe, alone or with others, nor 2
-- toes, nor all 5: 20 of the 31 possible sets (NOTES.md, Findings).
-- src:448 | * Cụt hẳn 4 ngón chân trong đó có ngón chân cái 20%
-- src:449 | * Cụt 3 ngón chân trong đó có ngón chân cái 15%
-- src:450 | * Cụt ngón chân cái 5%
GIVEN `the toes` IS A LIST OF `A toe`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A row of the permanent injury tables`
`the row for the amputation of the toes` `the toes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF n EQUALS 1 AND `with the big toe` THEN JUST `amputation of the big toe`
        IF n EQUALS 3 AND `with the big toe` THEN JUST `amputation of 3 toes including the big toe`
        IF n EQUALS 4 AND `with the big toe` THEN JUST `amputation of 4 toes including the big toe`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        n MEANS count (nub `the toes`)
        `with the big toe` MEANS elem `the big toe` `the toes`

§§ `The notes under the tables`

-- Ankylosis of the joints of fingers (other than the thumb and the index) and of toes (other
-- than the big toe): 50% of the amount for the amputation of that finger or toe.
-- For a finger set no row prices, or a toe other than the big toe (which no row prices on its
-- own), there is no amputation amount to halve: the injury is not in the tables (NOTES.md,
-- Findings). Ankylosis of the thumb, the index finger or the big toe is outside the note and is
-- likewise not in the tables.
-- src:453 | Trường hợp bị dính các khớp ngón tay (trừ ngón cái và ngón trỏ) và các khớp ngón chân (trừ ngón cái)
-- src:454 | thì số tiền bồi thường chỉ bằng 50% số tiền bồi thường theo quy định trong trường hợp cụt ngón đó.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fraction paid for ankylosis of the joints of a finger or toe` MEANS 50%

-- The second eye: an insured who lost one eye before the accident and now loses the other is
-- paid 100% instead of the 40% of the table.
-- src:456 | Trong trường hợp Người được bảo hiểm đã bị mất một mắt trước khi xảy ra tai nạn và nay mất nốt mắt
-- src:457 | còn lại thì mức bồi thường sẽ là 100% thay vì là 40% như được nêu trong bảng Tỷ lệ.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate for the loss of the remaining eye` MEANS 100%

-- Injuries not in the tables are paid by comparing their severity with the listed ones,
-- regardless of occupation; total loss of function of a limb or part counts as its
-- amputation; and (i) partial permanent injury is paid only from 5%, (ii) the Company has
-- full and unilateral discretion to decide the rate. The 5% rule is repeated as a paragraph
-- of its own; it is applied in lpa-benefits.l4.
-- src:459 | Những trường hợp Thương tật không được liệt kê trong bảng Tỷ lệ trên đây sẽ được bồi thường trên
-- src:460 | cơ sở so sánh tính nghiêm trọng của nó với những trường hợp khác có nêu trong bảng Tỷ lệ này mà
-- src:461 | không xét đến nghề nghiệp của Người được bảo hiểm. Bị mất hoàn toàn các chức năng của chi hoặc
-- src:462 | của một phần chi cũng được xem như là bị cụt hoàn toàn chi hoặc phần chi đó. Việc bồi thường theo
-- src:463 | đoạn này được thực hiện theo nguyên tắc sau: (i) Chỉ trả tiền bảo hiểm cho Thương tật bộ phận vĩnh
-- src:464 | viễn nếu mức độ Thương tật là từ 5% trở lên; và (ii) Công ty có toàn quyền đơn phương quyết định tỷ
-- src:465 | lệ chi trả.
-- src:467 | Chỉ trả tiền bảo hiểm cho Thương tật bộ phận vĩnh viễn nếu mức độ Thương tật là từ 5% trở lên.
@ref src 459-465: the rate for an injury not in the tables is the Company's to decide
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the injury is not in the tables, and its rate is for the Company to decide by comparison` MEANS
    REFUSE "the injury is not in the tables, and its rate is for the Company to decide by comparison"

§§ `The rate for one permanent injury`

GIVEN `the row`         IS A MAYBE `A row of the permanent injury tables`
      `the side`        IS A `A side of the body`
      `left-handed`     IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate for the row, if there is one,` `the row` `on` `the side` `with left-handedness` `left-handed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the row`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the injury is not in the tables, and its rate is for the Company to decide by comparison`
    WHEN JUST r  THEN `the rate read from` (`the rate printed for` r) `for the side` `the side` `and left-handedness` `left-handed`

GIVEN `the injury`  IS A `A permanent injury`
      `left-handed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate for the permanent injury` `the injury` `, the insured's left-handedness being` `left-handed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the injury`
    WHEN `an injury in a row of the tables` r s THEN
        `the rate read from` (`the rate printed for` r) `for the side` s `and left-handedness` `left-handed`
    WHEN `loss of the remaining eye, the other having been lost before the accident` THEN
        `the rate for the loss of the remaining eye`
    WHEN `amputation of fingers of one hand` fs s THEN
        `the rate for the row, if there is one,` (`the row for the amputation of the fingers` fs) `on` s `with left-handedness` `left-handed`
    WHEN `amputation of toes of one foot` ts THEN
        `the rate for the row, if there is one,` (`the row for the amputation of the toes` ts) `on` `the right side` `with left-handedness` `left-handed`
    WHEN `ankylosis of the joints of fingers of one hand` fs s THEN
        IF elem `the thumb` fs OR elem `the index finger` fs
        THEN `the injury is not in the tables, and its rate is for the Company to decide by comparison`
        ELSE `the fraction paid for ankylosis of the joints of a finger or toe`
             TIMES `the rate for the row, if there is one,` (`the row for the amputation of the fingers` fs) `on` s `with left-handedness` `left-handed`
    WHEN `ankylosis of the joints of toes of one foot` ts THEN
        IF elem `the big toe` ts
        THEN `the injury is not in the tables, and its rate is for the Company to decide by comparison`
        ELSE `the fraction paid for ankylosis of the joints of a finger or toe`
             TIMES `the rate for the row, if there is one,` (`the row for the amputation of the toes` ts) `on` `the right side` `with left-handedness` `left-handed`
    WHEN `loss of teeth` n d THEN
        `the rate for the row, if there is one,` (`the row for the loss of` n `teeth, replaceable by dentures:` d) `on` `the right side` `with left-handedness` `left-handed`
    WHEN `loss of part of the skull through its full thickness` a THEN
        `the rate for the row, if there is one,` (`the row for the loss of part of the skull, in square centimetres:` a) `on` `the right side` `with left-handedness` `left-handed`
    WHEN `shortening of a leg` c THEN
        `the rate for the row, if there is one,` (`the row for the shortening of a leg, in centimetres:` c) `on` `the right side` `with left-handedness` `left-handed`
    WHEN `an injury not in the tables` m THEN
        CONSIDER m
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the injury is not in the tables, and its rate is for the Company to decide by comparison`
        WHEN JUST r  THEN r

-- Which period of permanence an injury needs: 104 weeks for a total permanent injury, 52 for
-- a partial one (src 156-163). The remaining eye is a row of the partial table at a new rate
-- (fork F9); an injury not in the tables is assessed as partial (src 463-464 speak of partial
-- permanent injury).
GIVEN `the injury` IS A `A permanent injury`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a total permanent injury:` `the injury` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the injury`
    WHEN `an injury in a row of the tables` r s THEN
        CONSIDER `the part of the tables for` r
        WHEN `total permanent injury` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
